{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1284798-romancing-a-hob-goblin","id":1284798,"title":"Romancing a Hob Goblin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-04T13:55:53-08:00","id":1284798,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Romancing a Hob Goblin","content":"Is it possible for a changeling to fall in love with a Hob Goblin and/or vice-versa? If so, how would you, as an ST, handle such a relationship? I know there's a character in Night Horrors: Grim Fears (the Tikbalang), buuuuut--what are some important things to consider?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T16:51:37-08:00","id":1284845,"title":"","content":"Absolutely! Anything can happen in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> However, they're fundamentally creatures of different worlds. Goblins aren't human, even if they once were, and they rely on the Hedge to survive. They're much more bound by their role in the overarching story, have close ties to the Wyrd, and tend to operate on inhuman patterns of contracts and pledges. To adapt an analogy I've used before, it would be a bit like romancing an enormously complex artificial intelligence. It's possible, but they're very, very alien to you, and you to them, because they're fundamentally <i>not human</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T21:27:11-08:00","id":1285792,"title":"","content":"What Changeling in their right mind would even so much as humor the idea of romancing a creature from the Hedge?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure stuff like that is exactly what lead to them being captured in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T21:51:48-08:00","id":1285799,"title":"","content":"Damn misclick on my phone!<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically I can see a Changeling under the right circumstances hooking up with a Hedge Creature. It may be a toxic one way relationship, or just an unhealthy diversion from their problems, or it could be solace for a desperate loner. Some Changeling are really oogly and lonely. Some have horrible social skills and combine that with desperation some Hedge Creature that accepts them and doesn\u2019t care that they are paranoid and dress like a hobo and eat bugs and human flesh. It could work, don\u2019t underestimate desperation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T21:52:28-08:00","id":1285800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1284798-romancing-a-hob-goblin?p=1285792#post1285792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Changeling in their right mind would even so much as humor the idea of romancing a creature from the Hedge?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure stuff like that is exactly what lead to them being captured in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of Changelings are not in their right mind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T06:00:22-08:00","id":1285858,"title":"","content":"Also, nice hedge creatures exist. Like that one who's just trying to find the party who owns his old Hollow with a chain of deals, most of them mutually beneficial. Sure, he probably doesn't think like a human, but I could see people becoming friendly with him, sympathizing with him or even becoming attracted to him. Plus, I saw nothing in the corebook saying that romancing a Hob is a clarity attack, as long as you still spend time Ironside and have human friends.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Marrying a Hob could even be a way to cheekily justify purchasing Hob Kin<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: Tl:dr, if it looks humanoid and at least seems to think human, you can at least fall in lust with it. And if a Changeling can romance a Huntsman (if the legend in the core is true), why not a Hobgoblin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 02-08-2019, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T08:37:01-08:00","id":1286193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1284798-romancing-a-hob-goblin?p=1285858#post1285858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT 2: Tl:dr, if it looks humanoid and at least seems to think human, you can at least fall in lust with it. And if a Changeling can romance a Huntsman (if the legend in the core is true), why not a Hobgoblin?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who says it has to look humanoid? There's some pretty weird fetishes out there, you know? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T12:10:48-08:00","id":1286257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1284798-romancing-a-hob-goblin?p=1286193#post1286193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Who says it has to look humanoid? There's some pretty weird fetishes out there, you know? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also true. Slipped my mind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T12:10:48-08:00","id":1286258,"title":"","content":"Double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T10:02:17-08:00","id":1287574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1284798-romancing-a-hob-goblin?p=1285858#post1285858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if a Changeling can romance a Huntsman (if the legend in the core is true), why not a Hobgoblin?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also skeptical about the validity of that legend. The last thing I heard regarding Huntsmen is that they're the Fae equivalent to Meeseeks.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;We Meeseeks are not born into this world fumbling for meaning, Jerry. We are created, to serve a singular purpose, for which we will go to any lengths to fulfill! Existence is PAIN, to a Meeseeks, Jerry! And we will do anything to alleviate that pain!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T10:13:41-08:00","id":1287576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1284798-romancing-a-hob-goblin?p=1287574#post1287574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm also skeptical about the validity of that legend. The last thing I heard regarding Huntsmen is that they're the Fae equivalent to Meeseeks.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;We Meeseeks are not born into this world fumbling for meaning, Jerry. We are created, to serve a singular purpose, for which we will go to any lengths to fulfill! Existence is PAIN, to a Meeseeks, Jerry! And we will do anything to alleviate that pain!&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That has been updated. Now they are the natives of chaotic Old Arcadia, enslaved by the pacts of the Gentry. Normally, all they want to do is hunt through their magical forests, but when the Gentry want to hunt down a Changeling, they go to the forests and pull one of the Huntsmen aside. Then the Gentry rips out the Huntsman's metaphorical heart, hides it away from them within a certain Mortal's Dream Bastion and replaces it with one of their own Titles. This suppresses their desire for their natural Aspirations and replaces it with the Keeper's own Aspiration to recapture a specific Changeling. The Huntsman's natural Aspirations are entirely suppressed while Ironside. But when they are in the Hedge, you can try to reach their true desires and convince them to let you help them find their Heart, sealing the deal with a Pledge. <br /> <br /> Of course, not all the Huntsmen are nice naturally either. The one detailed in the Jumpstart's natural Aspiration? &quot;Behead his target&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:48:04-08:00","id":1288299,"title":"","content":"Suddenly, I'm tempted to play a what-if scenario where a hob goblins becomes human through the Wyrd power of love. Like how True Fae can turn mortal if they're exiled from Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T12:55:43-08:00","id":1290498,"title":"","content":"So the Huntsman just wants to hunt in a magical forest? So they could get along with a Hunter cell? Wait doesn't that mean mortal Hunters who sincerely love the Vigil quite possibly could go here as a kind of Afterlife/Hunter's Heaven if they died maintaining the Vigil and that befriended Huntsman took that individual to Old Arcadia? I also recall Arcadia being a paradise for heros in Greek Mythology. Looks like the writers are drawing upon that piece of lore as a possible explanation for later. Welcome to Hunter's Heaven... A Place where the Hunt will never end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T08:33:03-08:00","id":1294753,"title":"","content":"Dancers in the Dusk have Lady Ambrosia, and that shows how bad of a idea romancing a Goblin can be.. but that\u2019s first Ed.<br /> <br /> Then again, that is a good framework to use.<br /> <br /> Like what was said before, in all likelihood the relationship would be this toxic one sided affair... but it would be interesting. Like a train wreck in slow motion; beautiful in its horrible splendor!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T18:24:05-08:00","id":1294939,"title":"","content":"I can also imagine, going back to the Hunter, a sick, one-sided love ... The Hunter who &quot;loves&quot; his ptey...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T16:20:18-07:00","id":1297107,"title":"","content":"I don't see why people would think hobs are only like... devious or unhealthy things to be around, unable to be in a loving relationship. Some are sweet and loving, some are twisted, some are both. They're just weirdos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T18:59:14-07:00","id":1298250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1284798-romancing-a-hob-goblin?p=1284845#post1284845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely! Anything can happen in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> However, they're fundamentally creatures of different worlds. Goblins aren't human, even if they once were, and they rely on the Hedge to survive. They're much more bound by their role in the overarching story, have close ties to the Wyrd, and tend to operate on inhuman patterns of contracts and pledges. To adapt an analogy I've used before, it would be a bit like romancing an enormously complex artificial intelligence. It's possible, but they're very, very alien to you, and you to them, because they're fundamentally <i>not human</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't extend that to former human Hobgoblins like Goblin Queens that can become human again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T07:42:52-07:00","id":1298324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1284798-romancing-a-hob-goblin?p=1298250#post1298250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't extend that to former human Hobgoblins like Goblin Queens that can become human again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still would, honestly. Becoming a Goblin Queen fundamentally alters you, it's why it's so hard to go back. Becoming a human again is the focus of some grand and exciting story, not something that happens often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T11:33:17-07:00","id":1298371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1284798-romancing-a-hob-goblin?p=1298324#post1298324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still would, honestly. Becoming a Goblin Queen fundamentally alters you, it's why it's so hard to go back. Becoming a human again is the focus of some grand and exciting story, not something that happens often.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not that hard, just kidnap a child to take your place. And you still have you still have your intergity state. I think that the &quot;soulless&quot; thing is more for Hobgoblins that have never been human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T11:49:28-07:00","id":1299004,"title":"","content":"This idea fascinates me, so I need to go back and reread the stuff about hobgoblins so I can form a more complete opinion later.<br /> <br /> For now, I'll bring up Data, from Star Trek: The Next Generation as an example of a non-human, non-emotional being who (in at least one episode) explores the idea of a romantic relationship. What's interesting about it is how he's not motivated by love, affection or even attraction- he doesn't feel any of those things. But he still is capable of seeing value in a romance, and (in his own way) of trying to be the best partner he can be. So, just because something isn't human, and doesn't think like us, doesn't mean it can't find value in something like a romantic partnership.<br /> <br /> Second, if the relationship doesn't make sense from a Changeling perspective...it also doesn't have to make sense from a hobgoblin perspective, either. No matter what, it's not normal, so it's not hard to see the hobgoblin in question having strange quirks or an unusual (for them) attitude that leads them to entertain this concept. Maybe they're fascinated by how mortals aren't bound by contracts and deals, and can do whatever they want. Maybe they like the way the person walks, or talks, and to a hobgoblin that's as central to a person's identity as their actual emotions. Or something. Like I said, I need to refresh my understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}